# crontab -e, with <checkout> replaced by the path to this checkout. The
# watchdog keeps the current run alive (a host restart kills every process);
# the refresh
# moves to SQLite trunk's newest check-in nightly (and builds the pre-triage
# CLIs and checks the known bugs when it moves); pre-triage gives the current
# run's new findings a verdict every 30 minutes.
@reboot     <checkout>/case-studies/sqlite-coverage/deploy/watchdog.sh
*/5 * * * * <checkout>/case-studies/sqlite-coverage/deploy/watchdog.sh
30 4 * * *  <checkout>/case-studies/sqlite-coverage/deploy/refresh-trunk.sh
*/30 * * * *  <checkout>/case-studies/sqlite-coverage/deploy/pretriage.sh
